{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>A man.</b> I have only a man who made an valuation; a woman who made an valuation — from where? Scripture says: נפשת. יפלא — he shall separate. Nouns that have two forms in their explanation, and this one from that one, for we find ״כי יפלא ממך דבר למשפט״ — which is language of concealment. Like שן to דשנו. שרש and ושרשך. מסעף — ״פארה בסעיפותיו״, ״קננו״; and ״אחלצה צוררי״ and ״הלבש אותך מחלצות״." "<b>A vow by your valuation.</b> It juxtaposes valuations to vows: just as vows are under לא תאחר (you shall not delay), so too valuations are under לא תאחר, to pay them."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "The comment cites pairs of related Hebrew forms to illustrate roots appearing in different binyanim or with affixed letters. The passage is terse and catalogical; rendered as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:46.452537706Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}